WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.235 --> 00:00:01.670
- So today we're gonna be trying

00:00:01.670 --> 00:00:04.872
a really delicious ice
cream treat called Taiyaki,

00:00:04.872 --> 00:00:06.336
and I've brought some friends.

00:00:06.336 --> 00:00:08.445
- Hi!
- Hello, what up?

00:00:08.445 --> 00:00:10.949
- Salorme and Emily, here.

00:00:10.949 --> 00:00:12.684
And we're gonna get on the road

00:00:12.684 --> 00:00:14.443
and see what this thing is like.

00:00:14.443 --> 00:00:17.026
(upbeat music)

00:00:18.842 --> 00:00:20.535
- [Host] Taiyaki is a Japanese sweet treat

00:00:20.535 --> 00:00:23.219
that looks like a type of
fish called the sea bream.

00:00:23.219 --> 00:00:25.655
It usually consists of
pancake or waffle batter,

00:00:25.655 --> 00:00:27.646
and is filled with red bean paste.

00:00:27.646 --> 00:00:29.298
In recent years some versions have evolved

00:00:29.298 --> 00:00:31.973
to include delicious, delicious ice cream.

00:00:31.973 --> 00:00:33.445
The treat has been enjoyed by the people

00:00:33.445 --> 00:00:35.457
of Japan for over a century,

00:00:35.457 --> 00:00:37.605
so, we had to try it too.

00:00:37.605 --> 00:00:40.002
You told me ice cream is
your favorite dessert.

00:00:40.002 --> 00:00:40.879
- Could you say that again?

00:00:40.879 --> 00:00:42.226
I feel like I was doing this to my face

00:00:42.226 --> 00:00:43.816
while you were talking.

00:00:43.816 --> 00:00:45.367
- That's fucking unbelievable.

00:00:45.367 --> 00:00:46.200
(beep)

00:00:46.200 --> 00:00:47.706
- I like eclairs, too.

00:00:47.706 --> 00:00:49.721
But I guess isn't that
technically ice cream?

00:00:49.721 --> 00:00:51.085
- Eclairs are not ice cream.

00:00:51.085 --> 00:00:53.451
- No, they're like the ones
that are in the freezer.

00:00:53.451 --> 00:00:55.539
- She's talking about the
chocolate eclair ice cream bar.

00:00:55.539 --> 00:00:57.548
- [Salorme] Okay, so yes, Ice cream.

00:00:57.548 --> 00:00:58.879
Yup, I like ice cream.

00:00:58.879 --> 00:01:00.357
- What we're gonna eat
today is called Taiyaki.

00:01:00.357 --> 00:01:01.203
- Oh.

00:01:01.203 --> 00:01:02.132
- Do you know what that is?

00:01:02.132 --> 00:01:04.959
- No, I just said oh because
I don't know what it is.

00:01:04.959 --> 00:01:06.191
- How's my driving.

00:01:06.191 --> 00:01:07.024
- It's okay.

00:01:07.024 --> 00:01:08.109
We haven't died.

00:01:08.109 --> 00:01:08.942
- Okay.

00:01:08.942 --> 00:01:09.989
- It's ice cream time.

00:01:09.989 --> 00:01:11.310
- I'm so excited.

00:01:11.310 --> 00:01:12.393
I can't wait.

00:01:13.548 --> 00:01:15.624
- [Emily] This is so beautiful.

00:01:15.624 --> 00:01:17.272
- [Host] Did you expect it to be a fish?

00:01:17.272 --> 00:01:18.484
- No.

00:01:18.484 --> 00:01:19.371
This is so cool.

00:01:19.371 --> 00:01:20.328
I don't know if you can see it,

00:01:20.328 --> 00:01:23.599
but it's like this little
fish shaped cookie,

00:01:23.599 --> 00:01:25.881
and inside they stuffed it with Nutella.

00:01:25.881 --> 00:01:28.002
I got ube and black sesame.

00:01:28.002 --> 00:01:29.089
With sprinkles.

00:01:29.089 --> 00:01:30.749
- Okay, so I got the same flavor as Emily

00:01:30.749 --> 00:01:32.327
because I'm basic, but whatever.

00:01:32.327 --> 00:01:33.160
It tastes good.

00:01:33.160 --> 00:01:34.158
Don't judge me.

00:01:34.158 --> 00:01:36.297
- Um, I got ube and I got red bean,

00:01:36.297 --> 00:01:40.047
which is kind of the
classic Taiyaki filling.

00:01:41.368 --> 00:01:43.032
- Oh my god, that is so good.

00:01:43.032 --> 00:01:46.234
- Why isn't all food delivered to us

00:01:46.234 --> 00:01:49.484
in a delightful, animal shaped package.

00:01:52.077 --> 00:01:53.581
- I'm really glad we came.

00:01:53.581 --> 00:01:56.072
- It's like, sweet and a little savory.

00:01:56.072 --> 00:01:57.108
Yeah.

00:01:57.108 --> 00:01:59.517
But like, very very subtle.

00:01:59.517 --> 00:02:00.664
- Red bean is kind of sweet.

00:02:00.664 --> 00:02:01.736
Not too sweet.

00:02:01.736 --> 00:02:02.698
I really like these flavors

00:02:02.698 --> 00:02:04.014
because they're not overwhelming.

00:02:04.014 --> 00:02:06.620
Look at what I'm getting
all over my hands.

00:02:06.620 --> 00:02:09.505
- Oh my god, this is like a waffle.

00:02:09.505 --> 00:02:11.831
Dude, no cone can match up to this.

00:02:11.831 --> 00:02:13.860
- Get this thing.

00:02:13.860 --> 00:02:15.327
This thingamajigger.

00:02:15.327 --> 00:02:17.237
- I think we ate it the wrong
way because I saw everyone

00:02:17.237 --> 00:02:19.698
else eating it with a spoon.

00:02:19.698 --> 00:02:21.169
- I felt like I was stuffing it in my face

00:02:21.169 --> 00:02:22.807
so I could get to the fish part.

00:02:22.807 --> 00:02:23.640
- Yeah.

00:02:23.640 --> 00:02:25.615
- I just wanted that sweet fish meat.

00:02:25.615 --> 00:02:26.448
- Yeah.

00:02:26.448 --> 00:02:27.650
- You know, I think maybe
a waffle cone provides

00:02:27.650 --> 00:02:29.906
a little more structure,
but it doesn't provide

00:02:29.906 --> 00:02:32.717
as much fun as the fish cone does.

00:02:32.717 --> 00:02:35.036
- 'Cause its like having a
soft taco versus a hard taco.

00:02:35.036 --> 00:02:35.869
- Oh my god.

00:02:35.869 --> 00:02:37.719
- Everybody knows that soft taco,

00:02:37.719 --> 00:02:39.413
soft taco always trumps a hard taco.

00:02:39.413 --> 00:02:40.246
- Right.

00:02:40.246 --> 00:02:41.852
- They weren't so rich, they were like,

00:02:41.852 --> 00:02:44.371
very nice flavors all
blended together really well.

00:02:44.371 --> 00:02:45.368
- Yeah it just sorta like...

00:02:45.368 --> 00:02:46.368
- A wah wah!

00:02:47.350 --> 00:02:48.183
(beep)

00:02:48.183 --> 00:02:49.716
- So I guess you know,
if this is something

00:02:49.716 --> 00:02:53.417
that you can get in your
town, I definitely recommend,

00:02:53.417 --> 00:02:54.334
getting it.

00:02:55.195 --> 00:02:57.063
- Are you guys doing
anything fun this weekend?

00:02:57.063 --> 00:02:58.133
- No.

00:02:58.133 --> 00:03:00.550
(drum music)

